## Commits
### a4d45bc
refactor(core): cover reachable guards and delete dead ones

The lcov report for src/index.ts still lists eighteen unhit branches
and one unhit function after the reachable gaps were covered. Each one
is a defensive guard. Pin the ten that a public API or hook path
reaches with a test in the behavior file for its subject: an onError
hook that reads or writes state while the failed effect is still
current, state() on a hooked proxy, hooks on a frozen object, a derive
onDispose hook that writes a dependency, a recompute that disposes its
own derive before returning a promise, until() with a write or an
abort after the predicate turned truthy or with a predicate that
aborts its own signal, and an effect that disposes itself from a
re-run after a child threw on its first run. That last path clears
the effect's deps and reads before subscription update, so the
missing-maps return there stays: without it the re-run throws a
TypeError from removeStaleSubscribers.

Delete the eight whose condition cannot occur or whose guarded code
changes nothing: the identity and missing-set short-circuits in the
dependency comparison helpers, the wrapped-method return in the
hookless get handler (the typeof check above it already returns every
function raw), and the stable-dependency restore path after a re-run.
That path was reachable only when a nested first-run throw, caught by
the parent, had cleared the re-run state; the deps were then identical
to the previous run's, and removing stale subscribers, registering
new ones and reindexing reads on identical sets are no-ops.

Core-module coverage goes from BRH 522 of 540 and FNH 108 of 109 to
BRH 543 of 543 and FNH 108 of 108.


